d 'HDHETTEST': module to compute heteroskedasticity tests with exact Monte Carlo p-values for linear regressions with many regressors
d
d    The Breusch-Pagan and White tests rely on asymptotics with a
d fixed number of regressors p. When p is a sizeable fraction of n,
d    as with many indicator variables or fixed effects, they lose
d their nominal size (the Koenker version of the Breusch-Pagan test
d    becomes very conservative) and the White test cannot be
d computed. 
d
d KW: heteroskedasticity
d KW: tests
d KW: Bruesch-Pagan
d KW: White
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261110
d
d Author:  Yusuf Toyin Yusuf,  Kwara State University
d Support: email  YUSUF.YUSUF@@KWASU.EDU.NG
d
f hdhettest.ado
f hdhettest.sthlp
f hdhettest_example.do
f ../_/_hdhettest_display.ado
f ../_/_hdhettest_load.ado
f ../_/_hdhettest_mata.ado
